The task was to modify `last_used` in `crates/gptdisk/src/lib.rs` so that in case of a tie in `last_lba`, the entry with the smaller index is chosen.

The original code was:
```rust
        if best.is_none_or(|(lba, _)| last >= lba) {
            best = Some((last, i));
        }
```
This logic selects the last entry encountered when `last_lba` is equal to the current `best` LBA because of the `>=` operator.

To resolve ties in favor of the smaller index, we should only update `best` if `last` is strictly greater than the current `best` LBA. If `last` is equal to `best` LBA, we keep the one we already have (which has a smaller index because we iterate from `0` to `num_entries`).

I changed the condition to:
```rust
        if best.is_none_or(|(lba, _)| last > lba) {
            best = Some((last, i));
        }
```

I verified the change by running `cargo test -p gptdisk`, which passed successfully.

Summary:
- Changed `last >= lba` to `last > lba` in `crates/gptdisk/src/lib.rs`.
- Ran `cargo test -p gptdisk` and all tests passed.
